---
// How it works: the agent's section, the page's one tonal band. The three-sided story between the slab and the two
// paragraphs: played once when it scrolls into view, with "Play again" under it (`scripts/story.js`); on a phone,
// its five beats as a short list, with GitHub's side of it as a card. The scene is a picture to assistive technology,
// hidden from it: the beats are what it reads, at every width (visually hidden where the scene shows).
import { DOCS } from "../../landing/facts.ts";
import { githubPanelHTML, THREE_SIDES_BEATS, threeSidesHTML } from "../../landing/story.ts";
---

<section class="how" id="how">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="slab">
      <p class="label">How it works · built for coding agents</p>
      <h2 class="display">Your agent waits for the review, fixes, and stops when it is done.</h2>
      <p>
        Every review ends with a check on the commit and findings an agent can read. One command, <code
          >lookover wait</code
        >, does the waiting and says what to do next. Here is one pull request, from the agent's terminal to the merge
        button, with Lookover's own screen beside it.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="story" data-story>
      <div class="story-wide" tabindex="-1">
        <div class="ts-wrap" aria-hidden="true"><Fragment set:html={threeSidesHTML("story")} /></div>
        <div class="under"><button type="button" data-replay hidden>Play again</button></div>
      </div>
      <ol class="beats">{THREE_SIDES_BEATS.map((beat) => <li>{beat.text}</li>)}</ol>
      <div class="ts-card"><Fragment set:html={githubPanelHTML()} /></div>
    </div>
    <div class="after">
      <p>
        <b>The loop settles.</b> "Fixed" is checked on the new commit, never trusted. Nothing runs on half-finished pushes:
        the agent asks when it is ready. When the agent and the reviewer cannot agree, the check says a person is needed,
        and the agent stops.
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Works with the agents you run.</b> A skill makes the loop one sentence for Claude Code or Codex: "get this pull
        request through review". Anything that can call <code>gh</code> can do the same by hand.{" "}
        <a href={DOCS.codingAgent} class="ink-2">Setting up your agent, in the docs.</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
